invariant: INV-36
file: x509_ca.h
catches: test/zig-build-check.sh
reason: x509_ca.h declares ch_pubkey_from_pem in every build again, so a
  raw, webpki or server object, which compiles no x509_ca.c and defines
  no ch_pubkey_from_pem, declares it too, and a program that calls it
  compiles and then fails to link. chapulin.c is not translated from
  x509_ca.h for those objects, so zig-build-check.sh translates the header
  under each one's defines and refuses the default object's
  ch_pubkey_from_pem_tcp_blocking.

--- old
#if defined(CH_TRUST_CA) || defined(CH_X509_CA_TEST)
int ch_pubkey_from_pem(const uint8_t *pem, size_t pem_len, uint8_t der[CH_X509_MAX],
--- new
#if 1
int ch_pubkey_from_pem(const uint8_t *pem, size_t pem_len, uint8_t der[CH_X509_MAX],
